proftpd (1.2.8-11) unstable; urgency=low

 	Since latest 1.2.8 releases, a lots of patches coming from CVS have been
 	merged  in the  code,  so  that debian  edition is  less buggy  than the
 	official edition.  All  patches  are reported  in changelog,  along with
 	ProFTP bugzilla crossrefs.

 	All old  debconf craps^Wcode for anonymous  enabling/disabling has been
 	removed, so that postinst configuration  is less intrusive than before.
 	The  system  'ftp' user  is  also  always  added  by default,  even  if
 	disabled.

 	Maintainer scripts now manage  anyway some simple directives migrations
 	and also inetd|standalone modes as before.  Also they now are (and will
 	be)  written to  point known  configuration gotchas  and pitfalls  when
	needed.

	Hopefully, this new policy will satisfy the conscious sys admin.

 -- Francesco Paolo Lovergine <frankie@debian.org>  Sat, 23 Aug 2003 10:39:04 +0200

